  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Cone race 1v1",
  "description": "Place two cones near the sideline on each side of the basket, just inside half-court and about half a metre apart. Players work in pairs with one ball. The attacker stands behind the cone nearest half-court, the defender in front of the other cone facing the attacker.\n\nThe defender starts by running round the cones one way. As soon as they move, the attacker goes the other way, attacks the basket as fast as possible and finishes. The defender chases to contest the shot. The pair switch roles and stay on the same side; the pair on the other side go once the first pair are done. Switch sides halfway through.\n\nProgressions: cones further apart give the attacker a bigger head start, closer together forces finishes through contact. Let the defender fake, give bonus points for weak-hand finishes, or play first to five. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attack: keep your speed all the way into the finish."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Dribble and finish with the hand away from the defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Release the ball softly off the backboard – aim for the top corner of the square."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Defence: chase, get to a spot in front of the attacker and keep your hands high without fouling."
    }
  ],
